# Exceptions

Throw existing `app.exception.*` types. Map via `GlobalExceptionHandler` only. Body: `ErrorResponseDTO` (`status`, `message`, `path`, optional `errors`).

## Status map

| Exception | HTTP |
|-----------|------|
| `InvalidTokenException`, `SignUpNotValidException`, `LoginNotValidException`, `IllegalArgumentException` | 400 |
| `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, `HandlerMethodValidationException` | 400 (+ field `errors`) |
| `HttpMessageNotReadableException` | 400 (`"Malformed request body"`) |
| `ResourceNotFoundException` | 404 — ctor `("Article", "id", id)` |
| `ResourceAlreadyExistsException` | 409 |
| `BlacklistedTokenException` | 401 |
| `AccessDeniedException` / `AuthorizationDeniedException` | 403 (`"Access denied"`) |
| Unhandled | 500 — `Exception.class` catch-all in the same class (most-specific handler still wins). Prod body is `"Internal server error"`; other profiles use `ex.getMessage()` |

Do **not** add a second `@RestControllerAdvice` for 500. Two advice beans + `Exception.class` can steal 4xx mappings (Spring picks the first advice that matches, not the most specific across beans).

## Rules

- Prefer reuse over new exception classes.
- Do not return ad-hoc `Map` error bodies from controllers.
- `ExceptionHandlerUtils` already logs errors — do not double-log the same failure in every catch unless adding context.
